  "job_B8.1.4.3_20251003_114813": {
    "text": "Her ongyn\u00f0 seo \u00f0ridde boc, \u00f0e is genemned on Ebreis Uaiccra, & Leuiticus on Grecisc, & Ministerialis\nDrihten clypode to Moyse on \u00fe\u00e6re halgan wur\u00feungstowe, & \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0: Sege Israhela bearnum: Gyf\n& sette his hand ofer \u00fe\u00e6re offrunge heafod: \u00feonne bi\u00fe heo andfenge & fremiende to his cl\u00e6nsunge.\nOfrie \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t cealf beforan Drihtne, & Aarones suna, \u00fe\u00e6s sacerdes, offrian \u00fe\u00e6s cealfes blod &\n& hyldon \u00fea offrunga & ceorfan to sticcon.\n& don fyr innan \u00fe\u00e6t weofod uppan \u00feam sticceom \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6r tosnidene beo\u00fe, \u00fe\u00e6t heafod & ealle \u00f0a \u00feingc\n& waxan \u00fe\u00e6t innewearde & \u00fea fet; & se sacerd forb\u00e6rne \u00f0a Drihtne to leohte & to wynsumum stence.\nGyf seo offrung \u00feonne beo of sceapon o\u00f0\u00f0e of gaton, bringe enytre offrunga & unwemme.\n& offrie \u00f0a beforan Drihtne \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6s weofodes sidan \u00fee is on nor\u00fehealfe, & geoton Aarones suna \u00fe\u00e6t\n& tod\u00e6lon \u00fea lima & \u00fe\u00e6t heafod & ealle \u00fea \u00feingc \u00fee on \u00fe\u00e6re lifre clifia\u00f0, & lecgon uppan \u00feone wudu\nWaxan \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t innewearde: & se sacerd b\u00e6rn\u00fe hit eall uppon \u00f0am weofode to wynsumum\nGyf seo offrung \u00feonne bi\u00fe of fugelum, \u00feonne bringe he turtlan & culfran briddas, & offrie se sacerd\n& wurpe \u00feone cropp & \u00fea fe\u00feera wi\u00f0\u00e6ftan \u00fe\u00e6t weofod on easthealfe, on \u00fe\u00e6re stowe \u00fee man \u00fea axan\n\u00c6tbrede of \u00fea fe\u00feeru, n\u00e6s ne ceorfe, & b\u00e6rne hi uppan \u00feam weofode Drihtne to offrunge & to\n\u00deonne man bringe offrunge Drihtne, nime smedman & geote ele on uppan & stor, & bringe to Aarones\n& \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r to lafe bi\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t bi\u00f0 Aarones & his bearna.\nBring cl\u00e6ne ofenbacene hlafas mid ele gesmyrede butan beorman.\nTobrec hi lytlum & geote ele on uppan.\nNe do man nanne beorman ne hunig to nanre offrunga.\nBringa\u00f0 d\u00e6l \u00fe\u00e6rof & ne cume hit uppan \u00feam weofode.\n\u00deu scealt to \u00e6lcere offrunga.\nGyf he hry\u00f0eru offrian wille, bringe unwemne fearr o\u00fe\u00fee heafare.\n& setton Aarones suna heora handa uppan \u00fe\u00e6re offrunga heafod, & geoton \u00fe\u00e6t blod ymbutan \u00fe\u00e6t\n& bringon \u00feone rysle, \u00fee \u00fea heortgesidu mid beo\u00fe oferwrogen, to \u00feam weofode, & eall \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6rinne\nGif he sceap bringe, ramm o\u00f0\u00f0e eowe, syn hi unwemme.\nGyf he lamb bringe, Geoton Aarones suna his blod ymbutan \u00fe\u00e6t weofod.\n& bringon Drihtne \u00feone rysel & t\u00e6gl & gelyndu.\n& b\u00e6rne se sacerd hit uppan \u00feam weofode.\n& gyf man gat offrige, do man on \u00f0a ylcan wisan.\n\u00c6lc rysel sceal Drihtne to leohte.\nNe ete ge na\u00feer ne rysel ne blod.\nGyf se gehalgode sacerd synga\u00f0 & de\u00fe \u00f0\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t folc syngie, offrie Drihtne unwemme cealf.\n& l\u00e6de hit to \u00fe\u00e6s temples dura.\nNime \u00feonne of \u00fe\u00e6s cealfes blode & sprencge seofon sy\u00feon on \u00f0\u00e6s temples wahryft.\nGyf eall Israhela folc singa\u00f0 \u00feurh ungewiss, bringe an cealf to \u00feam temple, & l\u00e6de hit to \u00f0\u00e6re dura.\n& setton \u00fe\u00e6s folces ealdoran hyra handa uppan his heafod, & \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t cealf geoffrod sy, nime se\n& smite of \u00f0am sylfan blode on \u00fe\u00e6s weofodes hyrnan, & geote \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r to lafe bi\u00f0 \u00e6t \u00f0am weofode\n& b\u00e6rne \u00feone rysel uppan \u00feam weofode.\n& gebidde se sacerd for hi.\n& forb\u00e6rne \u00fe\u00e6t cealf butan \u00f0\u00e6re wicstowe.\nGyf se ealdor synga\u00f0, bringe anne buccan to bote.\nGyf folces man synga\u00f0 \u00feurh nytennysse & his gilt undergyt, bringe ane gat to bote to \u00f0am temole.\nGyf man wat \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er man swera\u00fe, he bi\u00f0 scyldig gyf he hit forhyl\u00f0.\nSe man \u00fee swera\u00f0 man & eft his gilt ongyt bringe an cylferlamb to bote, o\u00fe\u00fee gat, for hine & for his\n& gyf he nyten n\u00e6bbe, bringe twa turtlan o\u00f0\u00f0e twegen culfran briddas, \u00e6nne for \u00fe\u00e6re synne, o\u00feerne to\nGyf he n\u00e6bbe turtlan ne culfran, bringe melu.\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse, & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00fe: Beod Aarone & his sunum \u00fe\u00e6t hi bringon Drihtne to offrunge,\nNe ete nan man of \u00fe\u00e6ra sacerda offrunga, ac forb\u00e6rne hi man ealle.\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse, & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00fe: Ne ete nan man of \u00f0\u00e6re offrunga \u00fee man Drihtne bring\u00fe butan\n& Gyf \u00fe\u00e6r hw\u00e6t to lafe bi\u00fe ofer twegen dagas, forb\u00e6rne hit man \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0riddan d\u00e6ges.\nGyf hwa \u00fe\u00e6t smeru o\u00fe\u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t blod ytt, \u00fee bi\u00f0 Gode geoffrad, he sceal forwur\u00f0an.\nSe swy\u00f0ra boh & \u00fea rib sceolon beon Aarones & his sunena of \u00f0\u00e6re offrunga \u00fee man for\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse, & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00fe: Nim Aaron & his suna & heora reaf & smyringele & an cealf\n& gadera eall folc to \u00f0\u00e6s temples dura.\nMoyses dyde swa Drihten him bebead, & cw\u00e6\u00fe to \u00feam folce: \u00feis Drihten bebead.\nHe \u00fewoh \u00f0a Aaron & his suna.\n& scrydde \u00f0one bisceop mid linenum reafe & gyrde hine & dyde ymbe hine bl\u00e6h\u00e6wene tunecan &\n& band to \u00f0am rationale, on \u00f0am w\u00e6s awriten Lar & So\u00fef\u00e6stnys.\n& band his heafod mid cla\u00f0e & mid gehalgodan gyldenbende, swa Drihten him bebead.\n& he nam \u00f0one smyringcele, & smyrode \u00f0a halgan stowe & \u00f0\u00e6t weofod & ealle heora fatu & halgode\n& he geat ele uppan Aarones heafod & smyrode hine & gehalgode.\n& he scridde his suna midd & gyrde hi & hufode, swa Drihten bebead.\n& brohte an cealf for synne, & Aaron & his suna setton heora handa uppan his heafod, & offrodon hit\n& b\u00e6rndon \u00f0one rysle & \u00fea lundlagan uppan \u00f0am weofode.\n& \u00f0\u00e6t cealf hi b\u00e6rndon butan \u00f0\u00e6re wicstowe mid felle & mid fl\u00e6sce, swa Drihten him bebead.\nHi offrodon anne ramm, & guton his blod ymbutan \u00f0\u00e6t weofod.\n& curfon \u00f0one ram eall to sticceon.\n& forb\u00e6rndon uppan \u00feam weofode, for \u00f0an \u00f0e he w\u00e6s Drihtnes offrung.\n\u00d0a Moyses \u00f0one ramm offrode, he \u00e6thran mid \u00f0am blode Aarones swy\u00f0re eare & his swy\u00f0ran \u00f0uman\n\u00d0a he \u00f0us gedon h\u00e6fde, he geat \u00f0\u00e6t blod uppan \u00f0\u00e6t weofod, \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6r to lafe w\u00e6s.\n\u00d0one t\u00e6gl & eall \u00f0\u00e6t smeru & twegen lundlagan mid gelyndum, Hi forb\u00e6rndon uppan \u00f0am weofode.\n& \u00f0a he hi \u00f0us gehalgod h\u00e6fde, \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 he: Seo\u00f0a\u00f0 eowwerne mete beforan \u00f0\u00e6s temples dura &\n& swa hw\u00e6t swa \u00f0\u00e6r to lafe beo, o\u00f0\u00f0e of fl\u00e6sce o\u00f0\u00f0e of hlafe, forb\u00e6rne man \u00fe\u00e6t.\nNe fare ge seofon dagon of \u00f0\u00e6re stowe durum.\nAc healda\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6r wearde d\u00e6ges & nihtes, swa Drihten bebead.\nAaron & his suna dydon ealle \u00f0a \u00feingc, \u00f0e Drihten him bebead \u00feurh Moysen.\n\u00c6fter seofon dagum, Moyses clypode Aaron & his suna & \u00fea betstborenan of Israhela folce, & cw\u00e6\u00f0\n& beoda\u00f0 Israhela folce, \u00fe\u00e6t hi offrion for synne buccan & cealf & lamb, \u00e6lc anwintre & unwemme;\nHi namon \u00fea ealle \u00f0a \u00f0ingc \u00f0e Moyses him bebead, & brohton to \u00f0\u00e6s temples dura.\n& Moyses cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam folce: Wyrcea\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Drihten eow bebead, & Drihten eow \u00e6tyw\u00f0.\n\u00d0a Aaron geofrod h\u00e6fde & \u00f0\u00e6t folc gebletsod, swa Moyses him bebead, \u00f0a eode he ny\u00f0er; \u00f0a\n& com fyr of Gode & forb\u00e6rnde ealle \u00f0a ofrunga \u00fee uppan \u00feam weofode w\u00e6ron; & \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6t folc \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00deA namon Aarones suna, Nadab & Abiud, heora storcyllan, & on\u00e6ldon \u00fe\u00e6ron unhalgod fyr, \u00f0\u00e6t him\n& fyr com \u00fe\u00e6rrihte & forb\u00e6rnde hi to dea\u00f0e.\n\u00dea swugode Aaron & w\u00e6s sarig.\n\u00d0a bead Moyses Missabele & Elifafan, Aczicheles sunum, Aarones f\u00e6deran, \u00f0\u00e6t hi namon heora\n& hi eodon sona & b\u00e6ron hi aweg & wurpon hi ut, swa him beboden w\u00e6s.\nMoyses cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Aarone & to Eleazare & to I\u00f0amare, his sunon: Forl\u00e6ta\u00f0 eowre hreowsunga, \u00f0e l\u00e6s\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Aarone & to his sunum: Ne drince ge nan \u00f0ingc \u00f0\u00e6s \u00f0e man m\u00e6g druncen of beon\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse & to Aarone: Secga\u00f0 Israhela bearnum, \u00f0\u00e6t hi eton \u00fea nytenu \u00f0e heora clawa\nNe ete ge \u00fea \u00f0ingc \u00f0e ceowa\u00f0 & clawa ne tod\u00e6la\u00f0, swa olfend.\nHara & swyn synd forbodene to \u00e6thrinene.\nNe ete ge nanne fisc, buton \u00f0a \u00fee habba\u00f0 finnas & scylla.\n\u00d0a o\u00fere synd uncl\u00e6ne.\nNe ete ge nan \u00f0ingc hafoccynnes ne earncynnes, Ne ulan, ne nan \u00feingc hrefncynnes.\nNe h\u00e6me nan man wi\u00f0 his magan, Ne wi\u00fe his m\u00e6ges wif.\nHealda\u00f0 mine bebodu; ne do ge nan dingc \u00f0e \u00f0a dydon, \u00fee beforan eow w\u00e6ron, \u00f0e l\u00e6s ge beon\nArwur\u00f0ia\u00f0 eowerne f\u00e6der & eowre modor, & healda\u00f0 mine f\u00e6stendagas.\nNe stel \u00f0u, ne leoh \u00f0u, ne beswic \u00f0u \u00f0inne nextan.\nNe swera \u00f0u man on minum naman: ic eom Drihten.\nNe bysmra \u00f0u \u00f0inne m\u00e6g; nafa \u00f0u ane niht unforgolden \u00fe\u00e6s weorc \u00f0e \u00f0e wyrce.\nNe wyrie \u00f0u deafe; ne scremme \u00f0u blinde; ondr\u00e6d \u00f0inne God.\nNe dem nan unriht; ne forseoh \u00f0u \u00f0earfan; ne arwur\u00f0a \u00feone rican; deme rihte \u00f0inum nextan.\nNe beo \u00f0u sacful.\nNe hata \u00f0u \u00feinne nextan on \u00feinre heortan ac \u00ferea hine openlice.\nNe tyn \u00f0u \u00feine neahgeburas; lufa \u00feinne freond swa \u00f0e sylfne: ic eom Drihten.\nHealda\u00f0 mine \u00e6; ne do \u00f0u \u00fe\u00e6t nytenu h\u00e6mon mid o\u00feres cynnes nytenum: ne saw \u00f0u \u00f0inne \u00e6cer mid\nNe ete ge \u00fe\u00e6ra treowa bleda \u00f0e ge plantia\u00f0, \u00e6r \u00f0am fiftan geare.\nNe ete ge blod, ne ne gyman hwata ne swefna.\nNe ge eow ne efesion, ne beard ne sceron.\nNe l\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00feine dohtor beon myltestre, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00f0in land sy mid mane gefylled.\nNe gym \u00f0u drycr\u00e6fta ne galdra.\nArwur\u00f0e ealdne man & ondr\u00e6d \u00fee \u00f0inne God.\nNe hyrwe ge utancymene man, ac si he gemang eow swa inlendisc, & lufia\u00f0 hine swa eow sylfe, for\nHabba\u00f0 rihtne anmittan, & emne w\u00e6ga & emne gemetu & sestras: ic eom Drihten, eower God, \u00fee\nHealda\u00f0 mine bebodu & mine domas.\nGyf \u00e6nig man gelyfe on Moloches hearh, swelte he dea\u00f0e; h\u00e6ne hine man mid stanum.\nGyf hwa wirig\u00f0 his f\u00e6der & his modor, he sceal sweltan.\nSe man \u00fee bega wiccecr\u00e6ft, swelte he dea\u00f0e.\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse, & \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0: Sege Israhela folce; \u00feis synd \u00f0a dagas, \u00f0e ge sceolon Drihtne\nOn \u00f0am feowerteo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge \u00fees forman mon\u00f0es on \u00e6fen bi\u00f0 Drihtnes f\u00e6reld.\n& \u00f0onne ge in cuma\u00f0 on \u00fe\u00e6t land \u00fee ic eow sylle, ne ripe ge to cl\u00e6ne, ne ge ne gaderian \u00f0a ear \u00fee\nSum Egyptisc man gestrynde sunu be Israheliscon wife onmang Israhela folce; \u00fea flat he wi\u00f0 anne\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Drihten to Moyse: L\u00e6d ut \u00feone hyruwend wi\u00f0utan \u00fea wicstowe, & setton ealle \u00f0a \u00fee his\nSe \u00f0e man ofslyh\u00f0 o\u00fe\u00fee gewunda\u00f0, he sceal sweltan.\nSe \u00f0e orf ofslyh\u00f0, gilde heafod wi\u00f0 heafde.\nGif neahgebur wi\u00f0 o\u00feerne agylte, do him man \u00f0\u00e6t ylce \u00f0\u00e6t he \u00f0am o\u00f0rum dyde.\nGylde eage mid eagan & to\u00f0 mid te\u00f0, si he landes man, sy he utlendisc.\nIsrahela bearn dydon swa Drihten Moyse bebead.\nDrihten spr\u00e6c to Moyse on Synai dune, & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Sprec to Israhela folce \u00f0as word; \u00feonne ge inn\nSyx gear \u00f0u scealt sawan & wyrcean \u00f0inne wingeard & gaderian heora w\u00e6stmas.\n\u00d0\u00e6t seofo\u00f0e gear \u00f0\u00e6t land bi\u00f0 freoh \u00feurh Drihtnes gyfe; ne saw \u00f0u \u00feonne, ne ne rip, ne \u00f0inne\nNe heora w\u00e6stmas ne gadera \u00feonne hi weaxa\u00f0 sylfwilles, for \u00feam \u00f0e hit bi\u00f0 restengear.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t fifteo\u00f0e gear bi\u00f0 halig & forgyfenesse gear; on \u00f0am forgyfennysse geare man sceall freogean\nGyf he \u00feonne fram his hlaforde nelle, l\u00e6de man hine to \u00fe\u00e6s temples dura, & \u00feyrlie his eare mid\nNe swencea\u00f0 eowre magas: ondr\u00e6da\u00f0 eowerne Drihten, eowerne God.\nHealda\u00f0 mine bebodu & mine domas, \u00f0\u00e6t ge libbon eower lif butan \u00e6lcere sorhge.\nGyf hwa \u00feonne cwy\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t ete we on \u00feam seofo\u00f0an geare, gyf we ne sawa\u00f0 ne ne gaderia\u00f0 ure\nIc eow sylle mine bletsunga, \u00f0\u00e6t an gear bring\u00f0 \u00f0reora geara w\u00e6stmas.\nSawa\u00f0 on \u00feam eahto\u00f0an geare, & eta\u00f0 ealde w\u00e6stmas of \u00f0\u00e6t nygo\u00f0e gear & of niwe cuma\u00f0.\nNe sylle ge \u00f0\u00e6t land on ece yrfe, for \u00feam \u00f0e hit is min, & ge syndon utancymene & mine tilian.\nGyf \u00f0in wanspediga m\u00e6g beo mid \u00f0e, ne nim \u00f0u na mare \u00e6t him to hyre \u00f0onne \u00f0u sealdest.\nNe syle \u00f0u \u00f0in feoh to hyre.\n\u00deeah \u00f0in nexta for his yrm\u00f0e gange on \u00f0eowet, nafa \u00f0u hine for wealh ac for medgyldan.\nHi synd mine \u00f0eowas & ic hi gel\u00e6dde of Egypta lande.\nNabbon ge wealas ne wylna of eowrum cynne, ac of \u00f0am \u00f0eodum \u00f0e eow abuton synd, & of\nIsrahela bearn synd mine \u00f0eowan, \u00f0e ic ut al\u00e6dde of Egypta lande.\nIC eom Drihten eowwer God; Ne wyrce ge eow hearga ne agrafene godas: ic eom Drihten.\nGyf ge healda\u00f0 mine beboda, ic eow sylle fulle w\u00e6stmas & ge eta\u00f0 to fylle & ge eardia\u00f0 butan ege on\n& ic sylle sibbe on eowrum gem\u00e6rum & ge beo\u00f0 butan brogan; ic afyrre yfele wildeor & gewin fram\nGe feohta\u00f0 wi\u00f0 eowre fynd & hi hreosa\u00f0 beforan eow.\nFif eowre flia\u00f0 heora hundteontig, & hundteontig eowre flia\u00f0 heora tyn \u00f0usenda; eowre fynd fealla\u00f0\nIc eow geseo, & do \u00f0\u00e6t ge weaxa\u00f0; & ge beo\u00f0 gem\u00e6nifylde, & ic f\u00e6stnie min wed mid eow.\nGe eta\u00f0 ealde mettas o\u00f0 eow niwe cumon.\nIc sette mine halgan stowe tomiddes eowre, & ne awurpe ic eow.\nAc ic ga betwux eow, & ic beo eower God & ge beo\u00f0 min folc.\nIc eom Drihten eower Godd, \u00f0e eow ut al\u00e6dde of Egypta lande, \u00f0\u00e6t ge me \u00f0eowodon; & ic eom se\nGyf ge me ne gehyra\u00f0 & mine bebodu forhogia\u00fe, & mine \u00e6 & mine domas forseo\u00f0, & ne do\u00f0 min\nIc wi\u00f0stande ongean eow, & ge fealla\u00f0 beforan eowrum feondum & ge hyra\u00f0 \u00f0am \u00f0e eow hatia\u00fe; ge\nIc eow do seofonfealdne ege.\n& ic forbrece eowre ofermodignysse heardnysse, & ic gedo \u00f0\u00e6t eow bi\u00f0 \u00e6g\u00f0er heard ge heofone ge\n& eall eowre geswinc beo\u00f0 idele; ne bring\u00f0 seo eor\u00f0e eow nane w\u00e6stmas.\n& ic sende on eow wildeor, \u00fe\u00e6t forspillon eow & eowre nytenu.\nGyf ge nella\u00f0 onfon mine lare, & ga\u00f0 ongean me, ic ga ongen eow & slea eow.\n& \u00feonne ge fleo\u00f0 fram byrig to byrig, ic sende cwealm on eow, & hungor, swa \u00f0\u00e6t fif baca\u00f0 on\n& ic witnige eow seofon witon, swa \u00f0\u00e6t ge eta\u00f0 eowre suna & eowre dohtra fl\u00e6sc.\n& ic towurpe eowre heagan getimbru, & eowre hearga ic tobrece, & ge fealla\u00f0 betwux eowrum\nIc todrife eow, & \u00fe\u00e6t land li\u00f0 on reste, for \u00f0an \u00f0e hit ne reste \u00f0a hwile \u00f0e ge \u00f0\u00e6ron wunodon.\n& \u00f0a \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r to lafe beo\u00f0, \u00f0a beo\u00f0 on swa miclum ege, \u00fe\u00e6t hi fleo\u00f0 leafes sweg swylce hit swurd sy;\n& for eowrum agenum gilte ge beo\u00f0 geswencte, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t ge andettan eowre synna & eower yldrena,\n& ic ga ongean eow, & l\u00e6de eow on feonda land, o\u00fe eower ly\u00f0re mod ablysige; \u00f0onne gebidde ge\n& ic gime min wedd, \u00f0e ic behet Abrahame & Isaace & Iacobe.\nIc gyme \u00f0\u00e6s landes, \u00feonne ge hit forl\u00e6ta\u00f0; hit lica\u00f0 me, \u00feeah hit weste sy.\nIc eom Drihten eower God, \u00f0e eow ut al\u00e6dde of Egypta lande beforan ealles folces gesyh\u00f0e; \u00f0is",
